# Unstripped link output. app_process statically links the entire Android
# runtime -- bionic, Dalvik, skia, and now WebCore -- so with debug info it is
# roughly 200 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB hard per-file limit, and it crossed that
# line the moment libwebcore.a went in. It was tracked while it was small
# enough to get away with, which is not a reason to keep tracking it: it is
# pure build output, regenerated by scripts/build_app_process.sh, and what
# actually ships is the stripped ~13 MB copy that script deploys to the rootfs
# overlay and that sync_android_to_sdcard.sh puts under sdcard/. Both of those
# stay tracked.
build/app_process/app_process
build/app_process_qemu/app_process_qemu
# Same story, one rebuild later: app_process_debug was last rebuilt on
# 2026-09-12 (9.5 MB) and stayed tracked until the #315 rebuild linked WebCore
# into it too (199 MB, push rejected by GH001).
build/app_process_debug/app_process_debug
build/app_process_webkit_trial/

# Working files for a single session -- patch scripts, logs, captured tool
# output. Nothing here is an input to a build.
scratch/

# N3DS_UNTRACK_328: build output, logs, session notes and hardware traces are
# local-only. Everything below is regenerated by the scripts, or is a private
# working note / capture that names the developer's machine and network.
/build/
/toolchain/
/scratch*/
/scratch_*
/verify/
/evidence/
/captures/
/artifacts/
/old_zips/
/pipeline_*/
/generate_all.py
/wifi_trace.txt
# The flashable zip is a release asset, not source: build_sdcard_zip.sh packs
# it from sdcard/. The copy that used to be tracked here was a stale 2026-08
# zip with the old sdcard/ path prefix.
/sdcard.zip
*.log
/*.out
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.orig
*.orig[0-9]*
*.bak
*.rej
